@DorothyA-z9k Capitalism is absolutely an impediment to a better quality of life. The United States is a fantastic example of why late stage capitalism is an abject failure. Children go hungry, people die from lack of health care, science is directed by profit instead of by need and is limited by funding instead of innovation.

The only reason communism has failed so far is because of human greed and corruption. But with the advent of AI, we can build a new system based on resource redistribution where humans can work towards the betterment of society as a whole rather than resource acquisition. We need to move to a post scarcity model.

Here's a great example. Today, we have the technology to have limitless free energy for everyone. It would be simple to provide energy that is free for both homes and industry. We don't do it because it would disrupt the corporations that rely on profits to survive rather that have no energy bill. Data centers wouldn't be dramatically increasing the price of energy as a commodity which then crushes the population's ability to even be able to afford it. We don't because capitalism is good and socialism is bad. That's brainwashing. We already have roads, airports, fire and police departments, etc. Healthcare costs more per person with the current US model than it would if it was a single payer system based on taxes and free at the point of use. And the entire society would benefit from that. A healthy society is more productive.

