@TotallyNotKr3ative Error and failure are not interchangeable terms.
Here is a comparison with definitions from Webster to help you understand better:

"An error is a mistake, deviation, or incorrect action, often preventable. A failure is the resulting lack of success, or the inability of a system to perform its required function, often occurring when a mistake is executed. Errors cause failures, but not all errors lead to failure."

